00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.011
But I'm used to money a little different

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:15.056
than where you guys are starting to get used to money.

00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:17.892
Looking ahead at the next 25 years,

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:21.271
let's talk about this cryptocurrency.

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.189
We're gonna look at Tyrese first.
- [Obi Toppin laughing]

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.649
- We know, we talk about NFTs.

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:26.359
When we talk about this world,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.278
you're the first name that come up, Tyrese.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:30.739
Tell us how you got involved in this space

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:32.449
and teach me something, man.

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:34.284
I don't—I don't know a lot.
- We need your free knowledge.

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:36.411
- My older brother, Tanner,

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:38.955
he told me about NBA Top Shot.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:41.624
And he was like, it's basically virtual trading cards.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:42.500
And I kind of blew him off.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.544
I'm like, "Bruh, that sounds terrible."

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.087
Like, I like physical things.
- Yeah. Right.

00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:47.297
- You know what I'm saying?

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:48.798
And then, I was bored in my hotel room.

00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:51.217
We was in Chicago and I tweeted something like,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.220
"Dang, I missed the boat on Top Shot."

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.556
Like, "My moment went up $5" or whatever.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.099
Went to a team meeting, came back.

00:00:58.099 --> 00:00:59.225
It was up like 50. I was like—
- Ohhh.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.437
[All laughing]
- [Haliburton:] I was like—
- He just said, "Ohhh."

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:05.315
- [Haliburton:] Then from there, I became obsessed with this stuff.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:09.611
- NBA Top Shot was a substantial catalyst

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:11.946
to why NFTs are popular today.

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:13.114
I'm Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:16.868
I'm the CEO of VaynerX and an entrepreneur.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:20.205
It was incredibly commercially successful.

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:22.207
Dapper Labs, and with Roham [Gharegozlou] leading,

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:24.334
did a phenomenal job with that product

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.504
and really captivated the sports card collecting community

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:30.381
to get excited about NFTs in a frictionless way.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:32.675
The reason people are struggling with NFTs

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:36.096
is cause it's truly a profound new technology.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.556
NFTs stand for non-fungible tokens.

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:42.143
And we're all bringing our internet brain to the blockchain.

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:46.106
The blockchain is a new technology, decentralized servers.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.565
Nobody controls them.

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:49.067
Nobody owns them.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:52.028
What that allows for is the ability to show ownership

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:53.571
of something that's digital.

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:55.949
Somebody may say, why does somebody want to do that?

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.034
But we do that all the time now.

00:01:58.034 --> 00:02:00.120
When you think about NBA 2K

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.580
and you're buying some plus-ups for your players,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.832
you own that now digitally.

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:04.999
And when you put the video game in

00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:07.085
and you're playing 2K, 2K knows that,

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.129
and you're happy because you have a better team,

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.256
or something, or you're wearing cooler clothes,

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:13.424
but that's just in a closed environment.

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:15.093
The blockchain is the whole world,

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:16.970
the way the internet's the whole world.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.305
- So someone like me who don't know a lot about it,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.724
in my mind, you just have to get lucky.

00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:23.726
Like, is it a science to picking NFTs?

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:24.727
Is it a, like—

00:02:24.727 --> 00:02:27.897
