- One thing I guarantee you about the NBA

00:08:57.912 --> 00:09:00.748
in 25 years is that our tickets are NFTs.

00:09:00.748 --> 00:09:02.250
And I don't tell anybody who's watching this.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.459
You can go to eBay right now,

00:09:03.459 --> 00:09:05.795
search NBA tickets. Things sell,

00:09:05.795 --> 00:09:09.549
but the NBA didn't make any royalties on that transaction.

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:12.385
The reason the NBA will issue NFT tickets is when

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:15.638
that special night happens and it becomes collectible.

00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:18.057
As people are walking out of Madison Square Garden—

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:20.560
hopefully it's a Knick— out of Madison Square Garden

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.437
and they are literally listing or taking—

00:09:23.437 --> 00:09:24.772
you don't even have to list in blockchain.

00:09:24.772 --> 00:09:27.775
Like, they're taking offers on that NFT cause it sits

00:09:27.775 --> 00:09:30.361
on the blockchain and are literally hitting accept

00:09:30.361 --> 00:09:32.572
as they're going down the escalators and making money

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:35.408
because they pick the right night to go to the Garden.

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:36.492
That is profound.

00:09:36.492 --> 00:09:39.328
It's also profound because when I buy that ticket

00:09:39.328 --> 00:09:41.622
cuz I'm in L.A. watching and I'm excited

00:09:41.622 --> 00:09:44.959
that RJ Barrett Jr. dropped a hundred points in an NBA game

00:09:44.959 --> 00:09:46.335
and I need that collectible,

00:09:46.335 --> 00:09:48.004
I may sit on that for five years.

00:09:48.004 --> 00:09:51.716
And when RJ Barrett Jr. goes to the Hall of Fame in 22 years,

00:09:51.716 --> 00:09:53.467
that ticket might be worth even more,

00:09:53.467 --> 00:09:54.927
and I may sell that.

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:56.637
When I sell that for a profit,

00:09:56.637 --> 00:09:58.389
the NBA's gonna make a royalty,

00:09:58.389 --> 00:10:01.934
and every time that ticket is sold in perpetuity.

00:10:01.934 --> 00:10:06.105
The NBA is incentivized to turn every ticket

00:10:06.105 --> 00:10:08.399
into an NFT versus a QR code.

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:09.609
The fans that go

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:12.903
to these games are incentivized to have it to be an NFT

00:10:12.903 --> 00:10:15.114
versus a QR code cuz they can sell it.

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:19.201
This is a profoundly exciting moment that

00:10:19.201 --> 00:10:20.536
most people don't see yet.

00:10:20.536 --> 00:10:22.330
- When you buy the NFT, it feels like you have a part

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.582
of that athlete.  Like, you own this moment forever.

00:10:24.582 --> 00:10:25.416
You know?

00:10:25.416 --> 00:10:26.584
So I feel like it creates

00:10:26.584 --> 00:10:28.002
that fan engagement where they feel

00:10:28.002 --> 00:10:29.378
like they're even more a part.

00:10:29.378 --> 00:10:30.212
Cause that's what fans want.

00:10:30.212 --> 00:10:31.672
Like yes, they love watching us on the court,

00:10:31.672 --> 00:10:33.299
but they love to feel like they're part of our lives.
- Facts

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:36.719
So owning a moment, like, of your playing career is huge.

00:10:36.719 --> 00:10:38.638
So I think it's just gonna get bigger.

00:10:38.638 --> 00:10:39.847
- [Wade:] I guess the biggest question,

00:10:39.847 --> 00:10:43.684
what everyone wants to know, is NFTs here to stay?

00:10:43.684 --> 00:10:45.561
Or is it just for now?

00:10:45.561 --> 00:10:46.395
What do you guys think?
- [Barnes:] I feel like it's new, though.

00:10:46.395 --> 00:10:49.148
Like, it's like the new wave right now.

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:50.858
- Yeah. But I think it, I think it's here to stay

00:10:50.858 --> 00:10:52.985
because I think that's the future of our world.

00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:54.945
We're not gonna like print out prints

00:10:54.945 --> 00:10:57.657
of family photos and hang it on our walls.

00:10:57.657 --> 00:10:58.908
- Yeah.
- Like, I think people will do that.

00:10:58.908 --> 00:11:01.452
But I see the future as like big iPads

00:11:01.452 --> 00:11:04.955
on our walls that cycle through family photos

00:11:04.955 --> 00:11:07.291
and cycle through NFTs and art and all these different things.

00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:09.919
And on people's desks, when you walk in,

00:11:09.919 --> 00:11:11.671
they'll have little frames with NFTs on it,

00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:13.089
you know what I'm saying?

00:11:13.089 --> 00:11:14.423
I see that as the future of the world.

00:11:14.423 --> 00:11:15.800
- And I can't remember who said this,

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.843
but they said it was like when the internet first came out,

00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:19.220
like, there were so many different things.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:20.429
But like, if you got into

00:11:20.429 --> 00:11:22.807
the good ones, like Google, Amazon, like, those hit big.

00:11:22.807 --> 00:11:25.685
So like the NFTs, like, a lot of them won't, but the big ones,

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:28.396
like, they're gonna hit really big and they're here to stay.

00:11:28.396 --> 00:11:29.522
- [Haliburton:] This is the best part, though.

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:31.524
Like, when we ask each other questions about it,

00:11:31.524 --> 00:11:32.650
you know what I'm saying?

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.902
Like, that's I think is the best part is like,

00:11:34.902 --> 00:11:37.113
guys who were maybe afraid to ask me questions

00:11:37.113 --> 00:11:39.198
about what NFTs are aren't anymore.

00:11:39.198 --> 00:11:42.618
- A lot of the NBA players have been very aggressive

00:11:42.618 --> 00:11:47.039
with NFT land because I think NBA players are, by nature,

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:49.750
the most entrepreneurial, the most creative,

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:50.960
the most technically—like there's,

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:52.753
it's just the energy of the league.

00:11:52.753 --> 00:11:53.587
The days of players

00:11:53.587 --> 00:11:56.048
being incredibly one-dimensional is long,

00:11:56.048 --> 00:11:57.049
long gone.

00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:58.551
The thoughtfulness is profound.

00:11:58.551 --> 00:12:01.303
These players are making a lot of money now on the court

00:12:01.303 --> 00:12:02.471
given the great success

00:12:02.471 --> 00:12:03.889
of the league, and they're being thoughtful.

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:06.225
They wanna put those dollars to work in the right ways.

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:07.685
One of the things I'm most excited

00:12:07.685 --> 00:12:11.355
about is the first couple meaningful projects done

00:12:11.355 --> 00:12:15.234
by an NBA player that isn't specifically

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:17.737
in the concept of their name and jersey within it.

00:12:17.737 --> 00:12:19.780
Things that they're doing from the outside.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:22.199
And I think you're gonna see that and it's gonna happen.

00:12:22.199 --> 00:12:25.369
And when it happens, it's gonna create a ripple

00:12:25.369 --> 00:12:27.580
within the league that is gonna inspire other guys

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.416
in the league to do thoughtful projects

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:31.250
around their interests,

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:33.210
which I think leads to a better NBA player.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.879
I have empathy that owners

00:12:34.879 --> 00:12:37.173
and GMs may be scared about what guys are doing.

00:12:37.173 --> 00:12:39.633
I've analyzed with my ambitions to one,

00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:41.594
one day own the New York Jets.

00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:43.095
I've been analyzing guys for a long time.

00:12:43.095 --> 00:12:46.056
And I think a more rounded player is a better performer

00:12:46.056 --> 00:12:46.974
on the court.

00:12:46.974 --> 00:12:49.518
And so I'm excited about that chapter.

00:12:49.518 --> 00:12:52.772
- Everybody is like, at first is like,  "Eh, I don't know."

00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:53.773
- [Wade:] Yeah.
- You know what I'm saying?

00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:54.607
"I'm not with that."

00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:57.067
But like, even my mom and dad, like—
[All laughing]

00:12:57.067 --> 00:12:58.319
They're like, "OK, I'm trying to get in that now."

00:12:58.319 --> 00:12:59.361
You know what I'm saying?

00:12:59.361 --> 00:13:00.196
- Man, them two is good.

00:13:00.196 --> 00:13:01.030
I learned some stuff today.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.741
- [Toppin:] Aight, we need, we need to talk off camera.
- [Haliburton:] Yeah, yeah. [Laughing]
- [Wade and Collier laughing]

